dw_wdt: run the watchdog restart handler before PSCI's

On the SG2000 (badge) bl31 does not implement PSCI SYSTEM_RESET: the
PSCI restart handler (priority 129) never returns, so the restart
notifier chain never reaches dw_wdt's handler (priority 128) and every
kernel-initiated restart wedges the SoC with the console dead:
dm-verity restart_on_corruption at 1.5 s, `echo b > /proc/sysrq-trigger`,
panic=N. Measured on the bench 2026-10-17 (JTAG read of WDT_CR=0 and an
untouched WDT_TORR after the wedge). A plain `systemctl reboot` only
works because systemd leaves /dev/watchdog0 running at shutdown.

Run dw_wdt's handler first: it arms the watchdog with the shortest period
and the chip resets a few ms later, whether or not the PSCI call that
follows ever returns.

--- a/drivers/watchdog/dw_wdt.c	2026-10-11 06:27:50.000000000 -0700
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/dw_wdt.c	2026-10-17 03:08:08.572194635 -0700
@@ -650,7 +650,7 @@
 
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, dw_wdt);
 
-	watchdog_set_restart_priority(wdd, 128);
+	watchdog_set_restart_priority(wdd, 255);
 	watchdog_stop_on_reboot(wdd);
 
 	ret = watchdog_register_device(wdd);
